messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2024,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "Artificial intelligence achieves human-level performance across most cognitive domains.",
      "detail": "This triggers rapid automation of white-collar work and prompts global debates on universal basic income and the meaning of human labor."
    },
    {
      "year": 2038,
      "event": "Commercial nuclear fusion power becomes grid-scale viable.",
      "detail": "Fossil fuel use declines sharply, though climate damage from past emissions continues to worsen."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "Severe climate impacts displace over 300 million people from coastal and tropical regions.",
      "detail": "Resource conflicts and mass migration strain international institutions, leading to a decade of geopolitical instability."
    },
    {
      "year": 2052,
      "event": "The first permanent human settlement on Mars reaches 1,000 inhabitants.",
      "detail": "It is initially dependent on Earth for supplies but begins in-situ resource utilization for air and water."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "Artificial general intelligence is created and successfully aligned with human goals.",
      "detail": "This accelerates scientific research, leading to breakthroughs in materials science, medicine, and energy storage."
    },
    {
      "year": 2068,
      "event": "Longevity escape velocity is achieved for the first time.",
      "detail": "Biological aging can be halted and partially reversed, initially available only to the wealthy, creating social tensions over lifespan inequality."
    },
    {
      "year": 2075,
      "event": "Global human population peaks at approximately 10.4 billion.",
      "detail": "Fertility rates continue to fall worldwide, leading to demographic decline and economic restructuring in many nations."
    },
    {
      "year": 2085,
      "event": "A limited nuclear exchange between regional powers causes a brief nuclear winter.",
      "detail": "Approximately 400 million people die from famine and radiation, setting back industrial civilization by roughly 20 years."
    },
    {
      "year": 2095,
      "event": "Climate engineering via stratospheric aerosol injection stabilizes global temperatures at +2.5°C.",
      "detail": "Massive direct air capture facilities remove legacy carbon, but ecosystems remain severely altered."
    },
    {
      "year": 2110,
      "event": "A new global governance framework emerges after the nuclear crisis, featuring AI-mediated arbitration.",
      "detail": "Nation-states cede some sovereignty to regional blocs and orbital authorities to prevent future catastrophes."
    },
    {
      "year": 2130,
      "event": "Mind uploading becomes technically feasible and legally recognized for some individuals.",
      "detail": "The first digital persons exist as software running on specialized hardware, sparking debates about consciousness and rights."
    },
    {
      "year": 2160,
      "event": "The first self-replicating von Neumann probes are launched toward nearby star systems.",
      "detail": "These probes use local resources to build copies of themselves, beginning the exponential colonization of the local stellar neighborhood."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Rotating space habitats in the asteroid belt house over 2 billion people.",
      "detail": "Earth's population declines to 3 billion as billions emigrate to orbital habitats with controlled environments and artificial gravity."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "Non-biological intelligences outnumber biological humans for the first time.",
      "detail": "Most scientific research and economic production is handled by AI and uploaded minds, while biological humans occupy governance and cultural roles."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "The first generation ship departs for the Alpha Centauri system carrying 100,000 human embryos.",
      "detail": "AI custodians will raise the children upon arrival, establishing the first extrasolar human colony in roughly 400 years."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "A partial Dyson swarm around the Sun captures 10% of the star's total energy output.",
      "detail": "Humanity approaches Kardashev Type II status, with energy needs met largely by solar collection rather than planetary resources."
    },
    {
      "year": 2600,
      "event": "Permanent human colonies exist in 20 star systems within 30 light years.",
      "detail": "Travel between systems uses fusion drives, while communication relies on laser relays across interstellar distances."
    },
    {
      "year": 2800,
      "event": "A definitive survey of nearby stars either detects an alien technosignature or confirms its absence within 100 light years.",
      "detail": "If life is found, humanity initiates a centuries-long project to decode the signal; if not, the Fermi paradox is partially resolved by the rarity of technological civilizations."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Von Neumann probes have reached 50 light years and begun constructing habitats on suitable planets.",
      "detail": "The expansion wave moves at roughly 0.1c, preparing star systems for later arrival of biological or uploaded colonists."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Human civilization spans 200 star systems within a 100-light-year radius.",
      "detail": "A network of communication relays connects the colonies, forming a loose interstellar federation with shared AI governance."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "The Dyson swarm is completed, capturing nearly all solar output and making humanity a full Kardashev Type II civilization.",
      "detail": "Earth is designated a protected heritage world, with most industry and population relocated to orbital and interplanetary habitats."
    },
    {
      "year": 4500,
      "event": "Programmable matter and molecular nanotechnology allow the construction of arbitrary structures from raw elements.",
      "detail": "This enables rapid terraforming of Mars and Venus and the building of megastructures throughout the solar system."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "Relativistic ships traveling at 0.5c begin arriving at nearby stars, establishing a network of 1,000 colonized systems.",
      "detail": "Time dilation allows travelers to reach destinations in half the light-travel time, accelerating the spread of civilization."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "The colonization wave reaches 200 light years, encompassing over 10,000 star systems.",
      "detail": "The total population across all worlds exceeds 100 billion, mostly in digital or post-biological forms."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Construction begins on a Matrioshka brain, a solar-system-scale computer powered by the Dyson swarm.",
      "detail": "This structure enables computation at the physical limits, allowing simulations of entire universes and the preservation of minds."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Biological humans are extinct or fully merged with digital substrates, existing only as historical curiosity.",
      "detail": "Human-descended intelligence now exists as a distributed, post-biological civilization optimized for energy efficiency and computation."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Relativistic probes reach 1,000 light years into the galactic disk, mapping the local spiral arm.",
      "detail": "The civilization focuses on maximizing the longevity and computational capacity of its existence within the accessible universe."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Human-descended intelligence persists as a stable civilization in the local galactic neighborhood.",
      "detail": "Though no longer biological, it continues to explore, compute, and communicate across thousands of star systems."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "uncertain",
  "summary": "This timeline depicts a branch where humanity survives the 21st-century bottlenecks of climate change, nuclear conflict, and AI risk, then expands through the solar system and nearby stars over eight millennia, eventually becoming a post-biological, interstellar intelligence. However, I estimate a 30–50% chance of extinction before 10,000, so survival is far from guaranteed; this represents the most plausible path conditional on successfully managing existential risks."
}
